TSpeedButton.Alignment was added in Lazarus 3.0. TKASToolLabel derives from
TSpeedButton and only uses the value to pick a DrawText alignment flag; DC
never sets Alignment on these labels, so the LCL default (left) is the right
fixed value. Keeps 1.2.9 buildable with Lazarus 2.2.0.

--- a/components/KASToolBar/kastoolbar.pas
+++ b/components/KASToolBar/kastoolbar.pas
@@ -1330,7 +1330,9 @@
   begin
     Flags:= Flags or DT_RTLREADING;
   end;
-  Flags:= Flags or cAlignment[BidiFlipAlignment(Self.Alignment, UseRightToLeftAlignment)];
+  { TSpeedButton.Alignment exists only since Lazarus 3.0; DC labels are
+    left-aligned anyway, so keep that as the fixed default. }
+  Flags:= Flags or cAlignment[BidiFlipAlignment(taLeftJustify, UseRightToLeftAlignment)];
 
   DrawText(Canvas.Handle, PAnsiChar(LabelText), Length(LabelText), R, Flags or DT_NOCLIP);
 end;
